<title>AUSTRALIA: Qantas' Netherlands capacity confirmed.</title>
<headline>Qantas' Netherlands capacity confirmed.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Air Services Commission on Tuesday confirmed its draft decision to allocate capacity to Qantas Airways Ltd to operate three services a week to the Netherlands.</p>
<p>The commission also confirmed interim decisions to allow Qantas the equivalent of one Boeing 747 unit of capacity to Austria and an additional seven services a week to the United Kingdom.</p>
<p>Qantas planned to launch at least two new services to the U.K. from April 1998 with all seven new services expected to be operating by April 1999, the commission said.  </p>
<p>The commission said additional capacity had become available on the Taiwan route after Qantas decided to reduce its services.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
